No, Loglan had cases, similar to BAI, but not quite the same. For 
example you'd have a case tag that tagged "recipient" or "agent". So 
with dunda, you could use the recipient tag to mark the recipient 
instead of having to put it in dunda3. The difference is that these tags 
were much less specific and there were only a bit over 10 of these so 
more overlap occured.


